Change(genesis='e30427e699992327267add669c3bc989f6d16525ba6f493121eec7778638e0ce', deps=('803765d4eb3a5b4483c31457e052ce49077f95ada4312cb2f94855c112bc41a5',), event=Authored(todo='tiledlayout', at=datetime(2026, 11, 25, 8, 17, 6, 326523), actor='bmabsout', kind='todo', created=datetime(2026, 11, 22, 0, 0, 0), body="One general layout for the pages, on a phone and on a desktop from one model: the bar switches workspaces, a workspace is a tree of tiles and every tile is a page; on a wide screen the tree is a partition, on a narrow one the same tree is a stack with the focused tile full screen; opening a page beside another, resizing and going back are acts of one small algebra with laws, and the existing special cases (the list's pane, the secretary's panel) become instances of it.", spec=Flat(value=0.6), rationale=('The pages are already pure programs with addresses, so composing them is', 'cheap, and today each wide layout is written by hand in its page; the', 'owner proposed it.'), category='', waiting_on='', detail="State on 2026-11-22: a design note first, with the case against and a smaller version to compare; no code until the note is accepted.\n\nState on 2026-11-23: the design note is landed (release 2.1.224): one tree with one kind of node, the workspaces as the root's children, the bar as the root's crumb row, a pinned leaf for the secretary; six concepts where today's hand-made layouts have more. Stage a, the general module and its laws wired to nothing, is in work.\n\nState on 2026-11-23: stage a is landed (release 2.1.229): the general tiles module in the page framework, wired to nothing: one tree of pages, the acts, the arrangement for a viewport and the address, with one well-formedness check that the constructor, every act and the address parser keep, and fourteen generated laws. Stage b, today's layouts as instances of it with their hand-made code deleted, is in work.\n\nState on 2026-11-23: stage b landed (release 2.1.236): where a page stands is one arrangement; the list beside its todo, the todo's Back and the route against the width are instances of the tiles module, and their hand-made layout is deleted. Two tiles stand together wherever the room holds a list and a column (from a window of 856 px), under either chrome; a kept tile keeps its place through a resize and through Back. Left for later stages, each with its reason in the design note: the secretary's panel as the pinned leaf, the conversations column, the list's pane of the typeset pages, and the add sheet inside its tile. In the tests of this stage a few comments speak of its review and description: the next stage's pass removes them.\n\nIn work on 2026-11-23: the first half of stage c: a link between pages opens by the one rule, the divider drawn with its shares and dragged, the conversations column and the typeset list's pane as tiles, the window's layers above the tiles. The second half (hidden tiles kept and fed, the secretary's panel as the pinned leaf, the add sheet in its tile) follows.\n\nState on 2026-11-24: the first half of stage c landed (release 2.1.243): a link in a tile opens by the one rule, beside what is read on a wide room and in its place on a narrow one, and Back undoes it; the divider is drawn with its stops and dragged by a mouse, a finger and the keyboard, never under a least width; an open of a page the workspace shows focuses it. Left for the second half: hidden tiles kept and fed, the secretary's panel as the pinned leaf, the add sheet in its tile, the conversations column and the typeset list's pane as tiles, and the cause of a container query that broke two scenes.\n\nState on 2026-11-24: one scene of stage c's first half races on a loaded runner: it dispatches on a new tile's first child before the tile's page is mounted. It reddened one train of an unrelated change and was set aside there; the second half's change makes the scene wait for the page it needs.\n\nState on 2026-11-24: the first two points of stage c's second half landed (release 2.1.245): the conversations are a page of their own, beside a conversation on a wide room and above it on a narrow one, and the typeset list's pane is a tile; a page behind another keeps running, with its scroll and what is half typed, up to a bound the drawing states, and one machine says what a program undrawn may do. Left: the secretary's panel as the pinned leaf, the add sheet in its tile, the cause of a container query that broke two scenes, a clock for pages kept across midnight, and a small growth of the heap per open and Back that is not yet traced.\n\nState on 2026-11-24: since release 2.1.245 a held question on a phone sometimes comes to rest a few tens of pixels above its place under the header: one scene caught it once (the answer's room was sized to the whole window), on a train of an unrelated change, and passed on the train before. In work in the layout's next part: the cause, and a scene that forces the order that failed.\n\n2026-11-24: the first build of the secretary as a pinned tile was sent back after review. A pinned tile must not count toward a workspace's bound of tiles (a person's next open replaced one of their own pages), a link followed inside it must open from the page before it, whether the conversation talks about a page must be a reading of the store and not a hidden program on every page, and wherever it is drawn a control must hide it. In rework. The held question's place on a phone has its own change in flight.\n\n2026-11-24, release 2.1.251, deployed: a held question stays under the header. The cause was found by a scene that fails on every run: the bar that reports a sync left in the frame the question's round was drawn again, the browser's anchoring lost its anchor, and the question came to rest under the header by the bar's height. The place is now kept as a relation while the hold lasts, and ended with its room and its page. The secretary as a docked tile is in its fourth build after three reviews: the module's acts and laws are sound; the browser's doors are reduced to one, the header's button.\n\n2.1.254: stage C part three. The secretary is a page held at the end of the focused workspace (Hold and Release in the tiles library), with one door, the header's button, at every width; an open from the secretary's tile is the open from the page before it; whether a page has talk is a reading of the lines the device holds, with no fetch. Laws: a held page changes no act of a person; the secretary is erased by its absence. Remaining: the tiles as a library of their own.\n\nState on 2026-11-25: release 2.1.254 is deployed and was read on the live page at a wide and a phone width: the secretary beside a todo, alone with the todo behind it, and hidden behind the header's button. One fault found there and in work: on a device still syncing when the page opened, the secretary beside a page stays headed as having nothing about the page's subject after the lines that name it arrive.\n\nState on 2026-11-25, later: the heading fault is fixed (release 2.1.257). The secretary beside a page draws its heading from the last answer of its window alone: talk about the page's subject; none, a pull of the lines having ended whole; or none so far while the first pull still runs, which claims nothing. It follows the lines as they arrive, a turn as it is said and a rewind, with no reload, and a draft typed meanwhile stays.", source=None, subtodos=(), notes=(), note=''))